---
import EditorialLayout from "../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/hoodie-manufacturer.css";
---

<EditorialLayout
  title={"Custom Hoodie Manufacturer &amp; Private Label | Yauum"}
  description={"Custom hoodie manufacturer for private label brands. Explore styles, fabrics, GSM, printing, embroidery, labels, sampling and quality control."}
  canonical="https://yauum.com/hoodie-manufacturer/"
  jsonLd={[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://yauum.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Hoodie Manufacturer", "item": "https://yauum.com/hoodie-manufacturer/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Service", "name": "Custom and Private Label Hoodie Manufacturing", "serviceType": "Hoodie manufacturing and product development", "provider": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Yauum", "url": "https://yauum.com/"}, "areaServed": "Worldwide", "url": "https://yauum.com/hoodie-manufacturer/", "description": "Custom hoodie manufacturer for private label brands. Explore styles, fabrics, GSM, printing, embroidery, labels, sampling and quality control."}]}
  navCurrent={["/production/", "/hoodie-manufacturer/"]}
>
<!-- ============ 1 HERO ============ -->
<section class="pd-hero" data-od-id="hoodie-hero">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-hero-grid">
      <div class="pd-hero-copy">
        <nav class="pd-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Hoodie Manufacturer</span></nav>
        <p class="label">Custom hoodies / Private label development</p>
        <h1>Hoodie Manufacturer for Custom and Private Label Brands</h1>
        <p class="lead pd-hero-lead">Tell us what kind of hoodie you want to make. We’ll help you work through the fit, fabric, construction, artwork, labels, sample, and packing before you move into bulk production. You can start with a tech pack, a reference garment, or clear product photos.</p>
        <div class="pd-hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/contact-us/">Send your hoodie brief</a>
          <a class="link" href="#styles">Explore hoodie options</a>
          <a class="link pd-hero-inquiry" href="/contact-us/">Send an inquiry</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="pd-hero-media">
        <img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/hero-blank-pullover.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Blank pullover hoodie on a model as a visual style reference" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-hero-cap"><b>Product direction</b>Visual reference image · final specifications require confirmation</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="hero-rail" aria-label="Development scope">
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-label">Start with your references</span></span>
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-label">Check the physical sample</span></span>
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-label">Confirm details before bulk</span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 SECTION INDEX ============ -->
<nav class="pd-index" aria-label="Page sections" data-od-id="page-section-index">
  <div class="shell">
    <a href="#buyers"><span>01</span>Buyer fit</a>
    <a href="#styles"><span>02</span>Styles</a>
    <a href="#specification"><span>03</span>Specification</a>
    <a href="#fabric"><span>04</span>Fabric &amp; GSM</a>
    <a href="#decoration"><span>05</span>Decoration</a>
    <a href="#labels"><span>06</span>Private label</a>
    <a href="#workflow"><span>07</span>Workflow</a>
    <a href="#quality"><span>08</span>Quality</a>
    <a href="#inquiry"><span>09</span>Inquiry</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ============ 3 BUYER REQUIREMENTS ============ -->
<section class="section" id="buyers" data-od-id="buyer-requirements">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-buyers">
      <div class="pd-buyers-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">01 / Buyer requirements</p>
        <h2>What Do You Need from a Hoodie Manufacturer?</h2>
        <p class="lead">You need clear answers before you spend money on a sample or bulk order. We’ll help organize the product details, and we won’t guess at MOQ, price, timing, capacity, or certification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-buyers-list">
        <article class="pd-buyer" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <div><h3>Private Label Brands</h3><p>You may have a sketch, mood board, tech pack, or garment you already like. We help turn those references into clear decisions about fit, fabric, branding, and finishing.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-buyer" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <div><h3>Wholesalers and Retailers</h3><p>You need products that are easier to reorder and compare. Clear size, color, label, and packing records give both sides a consistent reference for future orders.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-buyer" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <div><h3>Sourcing and Procurement Teams</h3><p>If several people need to approve the order, one clear product record saves time. It keeps specifications, inspection points, packing, and delivery details in the same conversation.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 HOODIE STYLES ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="styles" data-od-id="hoodie-styles">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">02 / Hoodie styles</p>
        <h2>What Kind of Hoodie Are You Planning to Make?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Start with the silhouette. It affects the pattern, fabric, construction, and space available for your artwork. These images are style references, not completed customer orders.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-grid-4">
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-blank-pullover.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Blank pullover hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 01</span><h3>Blank Pullover Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A practical base for printing, embroidery, and private labels. Confirm the hood, pocket, rib, fit, and fabric before you approve the sample.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-full-zip.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Full zip-up hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 02</span><h3>Full Zip-Up Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A good option for layering, retail collections, or uniforms. Pay attention to the zipper, front alignment, pocket position, and hood finish.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-quarter-zip.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Quarter-zip hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 03</span><h3>Quarter-Zip Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">This style puts more focus on the collar and neckline. A reference sample helps explain the placket length, zipper, collar shape, and intended fit.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-oversized.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Oversized drop-shoulder hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 04</span><h3>Oversized Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Oversized does not simply mean choosing a larger size. Shoulder drop, sleeve volume, body length, hood scale, rib, and fabric structure shape the final look.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-heavyweight.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Heavyweight hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 05</span><h3>Heavyweight Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Choose this direction when you want a more substantial handfeel and stable shape. GSM matters, but so do the knit, surface, reverse, shrinkage, and rib recovery.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-cropped.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Cropped hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 06</span><h3>Cropped Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">The right crop depends on the customer and size range. Check body length together with width, sleeves, hem finish, and where the garment should sit.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-sleeveless.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Sleeveless hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 07</span><h3>Sleeveless Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Useful for athletic, streetwear, and layered looks. Confirm the armhole, shoulder width, edge finish, hood weight, and how the fabric hangs on the body.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-acid-wash.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Acid-wash vintage hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 08</span><h3>Acid-Wash Vintage Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A washed finish changes the base color, surface, and handfeel. Confirm the wash recipe, shade tolerance, placement, and appearance after laundering.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-camo.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Camouflage hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 09</span><h3>Camo Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Camouflage graphics need a clear repeat, color direction, and placement plan. Confirm how the artwork aligns across the hood, body, sleeves, and pocket.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-embroidered.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Embroidered hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 10</span><h3>Embroidered Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Embroidery adds texture and structure to the garment. Review the digitized file, stitch density, backing, placement, and how the fabric supports the design.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-graphic-screen-print.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Graphic screen-printed hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 11</span><h3>Graphic Screen-Printed Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Large graphics need a clear artwork file and placement reference. Confirm ink colors, print size, registration, handfeel, and wash expectations before bulk.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/style-puff-print.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Puff-print hoodie on a model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Style 12</span><h3>Puff-Print Hoodies</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Puff print creates a raised graphic surface. Check the artwork detail, expansion, edge definition, pressure, placement, and final handfeel on the selected fabric.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 CUSTOM SPECIFICATION ============ -->
<section class="section" id="specification" data-od-id="custom-specification">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-spec">
      <div class="pd-spec-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">03 / Custom specification</p>
        <h2>What Should You Confirm Before Sampling?</h2>
        <p class="lead">A hoodie is more than a front and back image. Confirm the measurements, fabric, construction, color, branding, and packing together. One change can affect several other details.</p>
        <a class="link" href="/contact-us/">Prepare a product brief</a>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-spec-list">
        <article class="pd-spec-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <div><h3>Fit, Measurements, and Grading</h3><p>Tell us who will wear the hoodie and how it should fit. A size chart, approved garment, or key measurements gives the sample team a clear starting point.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-spec-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <div><h3>Hood and Drawcord Details</h3><p>Choose the hood layers, panel shape, neckline, lining, drawcord, eyelets, and cord ends. Also check whether drawcords suit the age group and destination market.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-spec-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <div><h3>Pocket, Rib, Seams, and Trims</h3><p>Show the pocket shape, rib depth, seam type, topstitching, reinforcement, zipper, snaps, and other hardware. Small construction details can change both appearance and cost.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-spec-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <div><h3>Color and Garment Finish</h3><p>Share a color reference and the finish you want: clean solid, melange, faded, washed, or another effect. The actual process depends on the chosen fabric.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 6 FABRIC AND GSM ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="fabric" data-od-id="fabric-gsm">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">04 / Fabric and GSM</p>
        <h2>Which Fabric and GSM Suit Your Hoodie?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">GSM tells you the fabric weight per square metre. It does not tell you everything about warmth, softness, shrinkage, or quality. Compare real swatches as well as the composition, knit, surface, and finish.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-grid-3">
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/fabric-cotton.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Cotton fabric arranged as a visual material reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Material direction 01</span><h3>Cotton</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Cotton is often chosen for a natural feel. The yarn, knit, finish, shrinkage, color, and garment construction still need to match your product.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/fabric-fleece.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Brushed fleece fabric arranged as a visual material reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Material direction 02</span><h3>Brushed Fleece</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">The brushed inside can feel warmer and softer. Check the pile, shedding, thickness, recovery, and how it works with seams, prints, and embroidery.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/fabric-french-terry.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="French terry fabric arranged as a visual material reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Material direction 03</span><h3>French Terry</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">French terry has loops on the inside instead of a fully brushed surface. Compare the loop structure, weight, stability, and wash result on a real swatch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/fabric-polyester.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Polyester fabric arranged as a visual material reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Material direction 04</span><h3>Polyester</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Polyester may suit performance or easy-care products. Discuss stretch, surface, pilling, color method, moisture needs, and decoration before choosing the fabric.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/fabric-blend.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Blended hoodie fabric arranged as a visual material reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Material direction 05</span><h3>Cotton-Blend Fabrics</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A blend can balance handfeel, stability, durability, and cost. The fiber ratio matters, but the knit and finishing also change how the hoodie performs.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <aside class="pd-gsm" data-reveal>
      <strong>Not sure where to start?</strong>
      <p>Tell us the climate, season, fit, handfeel, artwork, wash expectations, and price range. Those details help narrow the fabric options before you review swatches and samples.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 7 LOGO APPLICATION ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="decoration" data-od-id="logo-application">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">05 / Logo application</p>
        <h2>How Do You Want Your Logo to Look and Feel?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Send vector artwork if you have it. Tell us the size, position, colors, surface effect, and wash expectations. Review a strike-off or decorated sample before bulk production.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-grid-3">
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-screen-print.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Screen printed lettering on a sweatshirt as a visual process reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 01</span><h3>Screen Printing</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Works well for bold spot-color graphics. Send the artwork size, colors, placement, and preferred handfeel so the print can be tested on your fabric.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-dtg.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Direct-to-garment printed lettering as a visual process reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 02</span><h3>DTG Printing</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Useful for detailed or multicolor artwork on compatible garments. Check the print color, pretreatment, handfeel, and wash result before bulk approval.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-embroidery.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Embroidered lettering on a hoodie as a visual process reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 03</span><h3>Flat Embroidery</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A durable choice for compact logos. Stitch count, thread, backing, edge quality, placement, and fabric stability all affect the finished result.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-chenille.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Chenille embroidered lettering as a visual process reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 04</span><h3>Chenille Embroidery</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Creates a raised varsity-style texture. Keep the artwork bold enough for clean borders and confirm the backing, garment weight, and embroidery details.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-heat-transfer.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Heat transfer lettering on a hoodie as a visual process reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 05</span><h3>Heat Transfer</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Can work for small graphics, names, numbers, or special effects. Check flexibility, edges, pressing position, finish, and wash requirements on the selected fabric.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/decoration-embossed.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Raised tonal lettering as a visual embossed effect reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">Process 06</span><h3>Embossed or Debossed Effects</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Choose this for a subtle raised or pressed effect. Feasibility depends on the fabric, backing, artwork detail, pressure method, and care expectations.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 8 PRIVATE LABELS ============ -->
<section class="section" id="labels" data-od-id="private-labels">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">06 / Private labels</p>
        <h2>What Should Carry Your Brand Name?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Your main label, size label, hangtag, bag sticker, and carton should use the same approved information. Confirm the wording, artwork, barcode, position, and attachment before production.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-grid-5">
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/label-woven.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Woven neck label as a visual private label reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">01</span><h3>Woven Main Label</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Send vector artwork and confirm the size, fold, colors, position, and sewing method. Review the label sample before it is used on bulk garments.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/label-size.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Garment size label as a visual private label reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">02</span><h3>Size Label</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Use the same size system on the garment, packing list, bag sticker, and carton. The label can be separate or combined with another label.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/label-heat-transfer.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Heat transfer neck label as a visual private label reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">03</span><h3>Heat Transfer Neck Label</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A printed neck label can reduce sewn-in bulk on suitable fabrics. Test the opacity, position, pressing result, comfort, and wear resistance first.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/label-pu-patch.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="PU brand patch as a visual private label reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">04</span><h3>PU or Faux-Leather Patch</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Patches can sit at the hem, pocket, or sleeve. Confirm the shape, thickness, color, surface effect, edge, and attachment method.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media"><img src="/uploads/hoodie-manufacturer/label-hangtag.webp" width="1248" height="1248" alt="Custom garment hangtag as a visual packaging reference" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">05</span><h3>Custom Hangtag</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Provide the final approved text and barcode. Then confirm the card, size, print, finish, string or fastener, and where the tag should be attached.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="pd-source" data-reveal>These label images are visual references. You must supply or approve the final wording, fiber content, origin, care instructions, compliance text, and barcode for your market.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 9 MOQ AND QUOTATION ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="commercial" data-od-id="moq-quotation">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">07 / MOQ and quotation</p>
        <h2>What Affects Your MOQ and Unit Price?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">There is no useful fixed answer without seeing the hoodie. Fabric, color, construction, artwork, labels, quantity, and packing can all change the MOQ and price.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-moq">
      <article class="pd-moq-item" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-moq-num">01</span>
        <h3>What Affects Your MOQ?</h3>
        <p>MOQ can change with fabric availability, custom color, washing, decoration, labels, trims, and your size and color split. Tell us the quantity you want to test and scale.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-moq-item" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-moq-num">02</span>
        <h3>What Affects Your Unit Price?</h3>
        <p>Price depends on fabric use, construction time, artwork, trims, labels, testing, packing, quantity, and delivery terms. A complete brief makes the quote more useful.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-moq-item" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-moq-num">03</span>
        <h3>How Do You Compare Supplier Quotes?</h3>
        <p>Send every supplier the same specification. Include measurements, fabric, artwork, labels, quantity, packing, destination, and trade terms so you are comparing the same product.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 10 SAMPLING TO BULK ============ -->
<section class="section" id="workflow" data-od-id="sampling-to-bulk">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">08 / Sampling to bulk</p>
        <h2>How Does Your Hoodie Move from Idea to Bulk Production?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">The goal is simple: make the product clear, check a physical sample, record your approval, and use that reference when the order moves into production.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="pd-flow">
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">01</span>
        <h3>Tell Us What You Want to Make</h3>
        <p>Share the style, quantity, target customer, references, fit, fabric, artwork, labels, packing, destination, and timing. We’ll identify what is still missing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">02</span>
        <h3>Confirm the Product Details</h3>
        <p>Before sampling, both sides should understand the material, measurements, construction, branding, sample needs, price factors, and expected project schedule.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">03</span>
        <h3>Make and Review the Sample</h3>
        <p>Use the physical sample to check fit, fabric, sewing, trims, artwork, and labels. The sample type and timing depend on the product.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">04</span>
        <h3>Send One Clear Set of Comments</h3>
        <p>Measure and wear the sample, then mark every requested change in one file. This gives the next sample or bulk order a cleaner reference.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">05</span>
        <h3>Move into Bulk Production</h3>
        <p>Once the sample and commercial details are approved, the order can move through cutting, sewing, decoration, finishing, checks, and packing.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 11 QUALITY CHECKPOINTS ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="quality" data-od-id="quality-checkpoints">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-qc">
      <div class="pd-qc-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">09 / Quality checkpoints</p>
        <h2>What Should Be Checked Before Your Hoodies Are Packed?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Agree on the inspection method, tolerances, defect rules, and report before production. The checkpoints below show what to plan; they are not a fixed AQL promise for every order.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-qc-list">
        <article class="pd-qc-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <div><h3>Check the Incoming Fabric</h3><p>Compare the material with the approved reference. Check identity, color, width, weight or construction where needed, surface condition, and visible defects.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-qc-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <div><h3>Check the Hoodie While It Is Being Sewn</h3><p>Look at key measurements, seams, stitching, pocket and zipper alignment, reinforcement, matching, and obvious workmanship problems during production.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-qc-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <div><h3>Check Artwork and Labels</h3><p>Confirm placement, size, spelling, color, direction, and attachment against the approved files. The buyer must approve all barcode and legal label content.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-qc-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <div><h3>Check the Finished Order and Packing</h3><p>Review garments, quantities, size and color assortments, labels, folding, bags, carton marks, and documents using the agreed inspection plan.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 12 PACKAGING AND DELIVERY ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="packing" data-od-id="packaging-delivery">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-pack">
      <div class="pd-pack-main">
        <div data-reveal>
          <p class="label">10 / Packaging and delivery</p>
          <h2>How Should Your Hoodies Be Packed and Delivered?</h2>
          <p class="lead">Tell us what happens after the cartons leave production. Retail, e-commerce, warehouse, and wholesale orders may need different labels, bags, carton assortments, and delivery documents.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-pack-steps">
          <article class="pd-pack-step" data-reveal>
            <span class="num">01</span>
            <div><h3>Pack Each Hoodie</h3><p>Confirm how the hoodie should be folded, bagged, labeled, and identified. Add inserts, warning text, stickers, or barcodes only when your sales channel needs them.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="pd-pack-step" data-reveal>
            <span class="num">02</span>
            <div><h3>Plan the Carton Assortment</h3><p>Choose solid-size or mixed-size cartons, units per carton, shipping marks, order references, destination labels, and the packing-list format.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="pd-pack-step" data-reveal>
            <span class="num">03</span>
            <div><h3>Confirm the Delivery Handoff</h3><p>Share the country, delivery address or port, target date, transport preference, Incoterm, and document needs. Freight cost and timing are confirmed for each shipment.</p></div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

