<!-- ============ 14 BUYER QUESTIONS ============ -->
<section class="section" id="faq" data-od-id="buyer-questions">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">12 / Buyer questions</p>
        <h2>Questions Buyers Ask Before Ordering Hoodies.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Start with the answers below, then confirm project-specific details in the quote, sample record, order documents, and production plan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary><span class="num">01</span><h3>What Should I Send for a Custom Hoodie Quote?</h3></summary>
        <p>Send product photos or a tech pack, your size chart, target fit, fabric or GSM preference, colors, quantity, artwork, labels, packing, destination, and target date. If something is undecided, tell us. We can separate confirmed details from open questions.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">02</span><h3>Can I Start Without a Complete Tech Pack?</h3></summary>
        <p>Yes. You can start with a reference garment, annotated photos, sketches, and key measurements. A complete tech pack is clearer, but missing information can be identified before an accurate quote or sample is prepared.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">03</span><h3>What Is the MOQ for Custom Hoodies?</h3></summary>
        <p>MOQ is confirmed for each project. It depends on fabric, color, washing, construction, artwork, labels, trims, and the size and color split. Send the quantity you want to test and your expected reorder quantity.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">04</span><h3>How Long Do Samples and Bulk Production Take?</h3></summary>
        <p>The schedule depends on the style, material, decoration, labels, sample type, revisions, quantity, packing, and season. Once these details are clear, the project can be given a more useful timeline.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">05</span><h3>How Do We Keep Bulk Production Close to the Approved Sample?</h3></summary>
        <p>Use the approved sample and written specification as the shared reference. Record measurements, materials, artwork, labels, approved changes, tolerances, and the inspection method before bulk production begins.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">06</span><h3>Which GSM Should I Choose for a Hoodie?</h3></summary>
        <p>Start with the climate, season, fit, layering use, price range, and handfeel you want. Then compare real swatches. GSM matters, but composition, knit, brushing, and finishing also change the result.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">07</span><h3>Can I Add Custom Labels, Hangtags, and Packaging?</h3></summary>
        <p>These items can be included in the product brief. Send final artwork, wording, dimensions, placement, barcode data, and packing instructions. Feasibility and minimums are confirmed for each item.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="num">08</span><h3>How Do I Start a Hoodie Manufacturing Inquiry?</h3></summary>
        <p>Send one focused product brief through the contact page. Include the style, quantity, sizes, colors, references, fabric, branding, destination, and target date. That is enough to begin identifying the next decisions.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

